---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout title="Talk Setup, AI Providers & Neural Voices" currentSlug="/guide/talk-ai-voices">
  <div class="space-y-8 text-buddy-text">
    <div>
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-buddy-cyan font-semibold">AI & Speech</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mt-1">Conversational AI & Neural Voices</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-buddy-muted mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        Equip Robo Buddy with an intelligent LLM brain, whisper speech-to-text, and local neural text-to-speech voices.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 2-Minute Quickstart -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">Two-Minute Setup Guide</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3 text-sm text-buddy-muted">
        <li>
          Open <b>Settings &rarr; Talk</b> and check <b>"Let him talk"</b>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Pick an AI provider from the dropdown:
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-1.5 space-y-1 text-xs">
            <li><b>Groq (Recommended Free):</b> Ultra-fast responses. Grab a free API key at <a href="https://console.groq.com/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-buddy-cyan underline">console.groq.com/keys</a>.</li>
            <li><b>Google Gemini (Free Tier):</b> Huge reasoning capabilities. Get a free key at <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/apikey" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-buddy-cyan underline">aistudio.google.com/apikey</a>.</li>
            <li><b>Ollama (100% Offline):</b> Needs no API keys. Install Ollama on your PC, pull a model (e.g. <code>ollama pull llama3.2</code>), and choose Ollama.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          Paste your key and click <b>Save key</b>. Your key is stored securely in <b>Windows Credential Manager</b> and is never written to disk.
        </li>
        <li>
          Click <b>Test</b> to verify connectivity. Then double-click Buddy on your desktop to start talking!
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Piper Neural Voices -->
    <div id="piper" class="space-y-4 pt-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">Piper Local Neural Voices</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
        Piper is a high-speed, local neural text-to-speech synthesizer. It runs entirely on your CPU with sub-100ms latency, giving Buddy a natural voice with zero cloud subscription fees:
      </p>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border space-y-3 text-xs">
        <b class="text-white text-sm">How to Enable Piper:</b>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-buddy-muted">
          <li>On the Talk tab, switch the TTS Engine to <b>Piper</b>.</li>
          <li>Click <b>Install Piper</b> (a one-time 22 MB download into your AppData directory).</li>
          <li>Download any voice from the bundled catalogue (e.g. Bryce, Ryan, Lessac) or click <b>Folder...</b> to drop in any compatible <code>.onnx</code> and <code>.onnx.json</code> voice pair.</li>
          <li>When Buddy speaks, his head and jaw nod along in rhythm with the synthesized speech.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <!-- Voice Models for Included Characters -->
      <div id="custom-voices" class="mt-6 space-y-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>🎙️</span>
            <span>Voice Models for Included Characters</span>
          </h3>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/tree/masa/piper_models"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-xs text-buddy-cyan hover:underline flex items-center gap-1 font-medium"
          >
            <span>Browse GitHub repo</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 opacity-80" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
          Pre-trained neural Piper voice models crafted specifically for Robo Buddy's included characters are available in the <a href="https://github.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/tree/masa/piper_models" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-buddy-cyan underline">JarvisChatBot Piper Models repository</a>. Each voice requires both the <code>.onnx</code> weights and <code>.onnx.json</code> configuration file:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-1">
          <!-- Arnold / Terminator Voice Card -->
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-card border border-buddy-border hover:border-buddy-cyan/50 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between space-y-3">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1.5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="text-lg">🤖</span>
                  <b class="text-white text-sm">Arnold Terminator Voice</b>
                </div>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-buddy-cyan/15 text-buddy-cyan font-semibold">T-800 Character</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
                Deep, mechanical Austrian cybernetic cadence. Matches the included <b>T-800</b> endoskeleton character for authentic Terminator one-liners, deadpan conversational AI, and audio responses.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-2 pt-2 border-t border-buddy-border/60">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                <a
                  href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/masa/piper_models/arnold-terminator.onnx"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  download="arnold-terminator.onnx"
                  class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg bg-white/5 hover:bg-buddy-cyan/20 border border-white/10 hover:border-buddy-cyan/40 text-[11px] font-mono text-buddy-cyan transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5"
                >
                  <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16v1a3 3 0 003 3h10a3 3 0 003-3v-1m-4-4l-4 4m0 0l-4-4m4 4V4"/></svg>
                  <span>arnold-terminator.onnx</span>
                </a>
                <a
                  href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/masa/piper_models/arnold-terminator.onnx.json"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  download="arnold-terminator.onnx.json"
                  class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg bg-white/5 hover:bg-buddy-cyan/20 border border-white/10 hover:border-buddy-cyan/40 text-[11px] font-mono text-buddy-cyan transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5"
                >
                  <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16v1a3 3 0 003 3h10a3 3 0 003-3v-1m-4-4l-4 4m0 0l-4-4m4 4V4"/></svg>
                  <span>.onnx.json</span>
                </a>
              </div>
              <div class="text-[10px] text-buddy-darkMuted font-mono flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>Model size: ~63 MB</span>
                <a href="https://github.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/blob/masa/piper_models/arnold-terminator.onnx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">View on GitHub &rarr;</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Rocco Voice Card -->
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-card border border-buddy-border hover:border-buddy-purple/50 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between space-y-3">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1.5">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="text-lg">🧔</span>
                  <b class="text-white text-sm">Rocco Voice</b>
                </div>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-buddy-purple/15 text-buddy-purpleLight font-semibold">Rocco 3D Scan</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
                Custom voice model trained to match the included <b>Rocco</b> 3D photogrammetry scan, delivering an expressive, natural personal desktop companion conversation.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-2 pt-2 border-t border-buddy-border/60">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                <a
                  href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/masa/piper_models/rocco.onnx"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  download="rocco.onnx"
                  class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg bg-white/5 hover:bg-buddy-purple/20 border border-white/10 hover:border-buddy-purple/40 text-[11px] font-mono text-buddy-purpleLight transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5"
                >
                  <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16v1a3 3 0 003 3h10a3 3 0 003-3v-1m-4-4l-4 4m0 0l-4-4m4 4V4"/></svg>
                  <span>rocco.onnx</span>
                </a>
                <a
                  href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/masa/piper_models/rocco.onnx.json"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  download="rocco.onnx.json"
                  class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg bg-white/5 hover:bg-buddy-purple/20 border border-white/10 hover:border-buddy-purple/40 text-[11px] font-mono text-buddy-purpleLight transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5"
                >
                  <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16v1a3 3 0 003 3h10a3 3 0 003-3v-1m-4-4l-4 4m0 0l-4-4m4 4V4"/></svg>
                  <span>.onnx.json</span>
                </a>
              </div>
              <div class="text-[10px] text-buddy-darkMuted font-mono flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>Model size: ~63 MB</span>
                <a href="https://github.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/blob/masa/piper_models/rocco.onnx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">View on GitHub &rarr;</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- More AI Voices Banner -->
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-xs flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <div class="space-y-0.5">
            <span class="text-white font-medium flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>🌟</span>
              <span>More Sci-Fi & Companion Voices</span>
            </span>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-buddy-muted">
              The repository also features <b>JARVIS</b>, <b>FRIDAY</b>, <b>GLaDOS</b> (Portal), <b>HAL 9000</b> (2001: A Space Odyssey), <b>TARS</b> (Interstellar), and <b>Bluey</b>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/MrSco/JarvisChatBot/tree/masa/piper_models"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="shrink-0 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-r from-buddy-cyan to-buddy-purple hover:brightness-110 text-white font-semibold text-xs transition-transform active:scale-95 shadow-sm"
          >
            Explore All Voices &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- How to Hook Up Downloaded Voices -->
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border space-y-2 text-xs">
          <b class="text-white text-sm">How to Hook Up Downloaded Voices:</b>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-buddy-muted">
            <li>In Robo Buddy, open <b>Settings &rarr; Talk</b> and make sure the TTS Engine is set to <b>Piper</b>.</li>
            <li>Click the <b>Folder...</b> button next to the voice dropdown. Windows Explorer will open your local voice directory (<code class="text-buddy-cyan">%APPDATA%\com.rocco.robobuddy\piper\voices\</code>).</li>
            <li>Drop both the <code>.onnx</code> and <code>.onnx.json</code> files into that folder (e.g. <code>arnold-terminator.onnx</code> + <code>arnold-terminator.onnx.json</code>).</li>
            <li>Robo Buddy automatically detects the new models in the Piper Voice dropdown! Select the voice and click <b>Test voice</b>.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Live Voice Duplex -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">OpenAI GPT-Live Full-Duplex Voice</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
        Under Engine &rarr; <b>Live voice</b>, you can connect an OpenAI API key for real-time bidirectional voice chat. You can speak naturally, and Buddy will listen, think, and speak back with real-time inflection—allowing you to interrupt him mid-sentence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Commands Table -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">Voice & Chat Commands</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
        Buddy understands natural intent and directly executes action commands when spoken or typed:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs font-mono">
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border text-buddy-cyan">"dance"</div>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border text-buddy-cyan">"do the chicken dance"</div>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border text-buddy-cyan">"climb"</div>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border text-buddy-cyan">"go to sleep"</div>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border text-buddy-cyan">"wake up"</div>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border text-buddy-cyan">"be quiet for 15 min"</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation -->
    <div class="pt-6 border-t border-buddy-border flex justify-between">
      <a href="/guide/screensaver-havoc" class="text-xs text-buddy-darkMuted hover:text-buddy-cyan transition-colors">&larr; Back: Screensaver Havoc</a>
      <a href="/guide/custom-characters" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-xl bg-buddy-cyan/15 hover:bg-buddy-cyan/25 border border-buddy-cyan/30 text-buddy-cyan text-xs font-semibold transition-colors">
        <span>Next: Custom Characters</span>
        <span>&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
